The scripts ran from .build/case/kbuild-probe/scratch/k1-dispositions/ and
are copied, with the build log, under .evidence/k1-dispositions-20261013/scripts/.
To replay, restore smc-build.sh as smc/build.sh and the scripts/ files in that
scratch layout, run smc/build.sh in the sealed image (mounts as in its
header), create the scratch disk with mke2fs -t ext4 -b 1024 ... 65536, then:
  python3 .build/case/kbuild-probe/scratch/k1-dispositions/scripts/smc_flights.py CAPTURE LANE
with LANE tcg-cortex-a72, hvf-host, tcg-single-cortex-a72 or
tcg-single-icount-cortex-a72. The MT-TCG, HVF and host-clock ST runs used
driver 8fcd34193f3a68ed739b7f4e23d38141fa922113e3029ae28a355904a62aa0d7.
The fixed-clock run used the retained
25873451ad575e666bd9115aef994243fcc4f9933e3059b3a25a9d8e9904744b, which
adds only that lane name. Later lanes in the copied diagnostic contract
serve the K01 proxy (k01-sched-ext-timeout-diagnosis.out).
